# Theme Rules

Reference: `Documents/decisions/theme-engine.md`

## Stack

Tailwind + Metronic demo1 layout + Augmentik theme CSS + Shadcn (`@/components/ui/*`).

Import order lives in `Project-X-Frontend/src/styles/globals.css`.

## Token conventions

- Dark tokens: `--ax-bg-main`, `--ax-accent-blue`, etc. scoped to `.dark` / `html.dark`.
- Light mode: `html.light` hybrid (sidebar may stay dark per `augmentik-light-theme.css`).
- Shadcn HSL vars in `shadcn.ui.css` map to Augmentik tokens.
- Module-specific overrides: `messages-dark-theme.css`, `ax-popup-dark-theme.css`.
- Default theme mode: `dark` (`settings.config.js`).

## React Native

- Import `{ colors } from '../theme/colors'` — no CSS variables in RN.
- Keep mobile palette aligned with portal dark tokens; don't duplicate ad-hoc hex values.

## Do's

- Add new surface colors as `--ax-*` in augmentik theme files, then wire through `shadcn.ui.css` if Shadcn components need them.
- Use `ThemeHandler` in `App.jsx` to toggle `html.dark` / `html.light`.
- Scope route-specific overrides (e.g. public interview pages skip global theme handler).

## Don'ts

- Don't add global unscoped color rules that affect both `.dark` and `.light`.
- Don't hardcode hex in new frontend components when a `--ax-*` or Shadcn token exists.
- Don't break light theme when editing dark-only rules.
